Package: bulknull
Title: Assessing Whether a Bulk-Null Result Can Distinguish Cell-State
    Dilution from Genuine Absence
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Itika", "Arora", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "itiarora@alfaisal.edu"),
    person("Ahmed", "Yaqinuddin", role = "aut",
           email = "ayqinuddin@alfaisal.edu"),
    person("Alfaisal University", role = "cph"))
Description: Diagnostics for bulk transcriptomic null results in studies that
    also have single-cell data. Computes a Dilution Discordance Score, the
    posterior probability that a non-significant bulk effect reflects dilution
    of a small subcluster rather than genuine absence, together with a
    Diagnosability Index quantifying whether the study design has power to make
    that distinction at all. Includes an applicability gate that refuses
    bulk-significant inputs.
